// 2sl drums: the pattern engine. Generated by src/2sl-drums.py from src/2sl-drums-brain.template.js and
// src/2sl-drums-functions.js (the functions); edit there.
// The design is the user's (PLANS/2026-10-15-2sl-drums-knobs.md, on PLANS/2026-10-15-2sl-drums-functions.md's
// function model): pure functions make patterns, the device keeps their history p0..pt.
//   - Voice picks one row or all; Function the generator or modifier; Seed walks the function's variants
//     (every combination of its settings, src/2sl-drums-functions.js). Seed and the settings are one state:
//     turning one moves the others' Live parameters (outlet 5), and the echo of a value sent changes nothing.
//   - Turning Seed or a setting applies the function live, with no Run: the first turn after a commit takes the
//     pattern as it is as the base, and every turn shows f(base, position) on the target rows, the starting
//     position too (the base itself comes back by Undo, or by a modifier's settings that change nothing).
//   - Moving Voice or Function commits what is shown as one history step; it is the next base. A hand edit
//     commits first, then is a step of its own. Undo drops what isn't committed (the settings go back to where
//     the turning started), else steps back one commit. No redo. The history keeps the last HISTORY_LIMIT.
// Playback is plain: each step plays at its grade's velocity (GRADE_VELOCITY), with the 909's shuffle.
//
//   in 0: MIDI note lists (pitch velocity) from the track: play a voice now (GM drum notes)
//   in 1: control messages
//     voice i         the row the function changes (VOICES order); VOICES.length = all
//     function i      the function (FUNCTIONS order)
//     seed x          0-100: how far through the function's variants (Seed)
//     param f p x     function f's setting p is x (one Live parameter per setting, built from FUNCTIONS)
//     undo            drop what isn't committed, else step back
//     clear           the row(s) Voice picks become rests: commits first, then one step (none if nothing changes)
//     name_click v    a click on voice v's name: Voice picks v (v again, or on all: see voiceOfNameClick)
//     edit v s [g]    a click on a step: rest/ghost -> hit -> accent -> rest; with g, set grade g
//     swing i         0-6 = the 909's shuffle 1-7
//     steps_<voice>_a n / steps_<voice>_b n   the pattern as stored with the set (steps 1-8 / 9-16, 2 bits each)
//     tick ticks / playing i / tempo f   Live's transport (the kit's clock)
//     ready           Live has finished restoring the set: the history starts from the restored pattern
//     stop            the Stop button: the displays forget the playhead
// out 0: to gen~: `delay_<voice> ms` then `trig_<voice> serial+velocity/2` per hit
// out 1: to the grid display    out 2: to the status display    out 3: hits, to the mix and voice displays
// out 4: stored values (route to the hidden parameters)
// out 5: `<scripting name> value` to the Live parameters Voice, Seed and the settings (route to each)
inlets = 2;
outlets = 6;

